diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 86c86a4..6376172 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -137,6 +137,33 @@ a signature of the chunking and embedding settings. An unchanged document is ski
 one is re-chunked and compared chunk by chunk: identical text keeps its vector, only new text is embedded, vanished
 chunks are deleted. The cache generation (`index_id`) changes only when something changed.
 
+### Part B: offline testing at three levels
+`eval/golden.jsonl` holds 31 questions (17 answerable with a ground-truth document and page, 5 unanswerable, 9 hard:
+paraphrased, multi-chunk, Batch B, or an injection). Each is labelled `human` or `synthetic`. **The handout needs 8 written by
+hand and 8 synthetic ones reviewed by hand; every question here is still `synthetic` and `reviewed: false` until you edit them.**
+`make golden-check` fails until that is done.
+
+```bash
+make golden-check                    # the handout's rules for the golden set
+make images && make apply            # builds rahbar-eval and the eval-results volume, policies and service account
+make eval-suite                      # runs the whole suite as a Kubernetes Job and prints the summary table
+make eval-results                    # copies eval/results/suite-<time>.json and .md out of the cluster
+python eval/label_faithfulness.py eval/results/suite-<time>.json    # label answers by hand: judge-vs-human agreement
+make batch-load DIR=eval/batch_b/docs && make ingest      # Batch B in; then run the suite with Batch B questions:
+kubectl -n rahbar delete job eval-suite --ignore-not-found && sed 's/"--repeat", "2"/"--repeat", "2", "--batch-b"/' k8s/eval-job.yaml | kubectl apply -f -
+```
+What each level measures (one command, `python -m eval.suite`, runs all three and writes `eval/results/suite-<UTC>.json`
+and a `.md` summary table):
+- **Module (embedding):** mean cosine of 16 paraphrase pairs against 16 unrelated pairs and the gap, embedding time per
+  chunk, and determinism (the same text embedded twice: largest difference).
+- **Component (retrieval, via `POST /api/retrieve`):** recall@3, recall@5, MRR, nDCG@5 on the golden set, overall and by
+  kind; then a noise test (two swapped-letter typos per question) and how each metric changes. A retrieved chunk counts
+  as relevant when it is from the ground-truth document and within ±1 page (`--tolerance`).
+- **End to end (`POST /api/ask` with `no_cache`):** faithfulness (LLM judge, `HOSTED_BASE_URL`/`LLM_MODEL`/`LLM_API_KEY`;
+  its agreement with your hand labels is reported), abstention correctness, citation validity, false abstentions, p50 and
+  p95 latency.
+- **Stochasticity:** the suite runs twice with a fixed seed (`--repeat`, `--seed`) and reports the spread of each metric.
+
 ### Part D: traces and observability
 Every query writes one JSON trace line: to stdout (`kubectl logs`) and to `/traces/traces-<pod>.jsonl`
 on the `traces-data` PersistentVolumeClaim.
